{
 "comment": "Vocabulary and characters, one rule per voucher. Every v voucher pays rent from Bank A. v01 to v28 write each of the 55 words that never count as part of a name, two per narration (one on the last), before and after Lambda Traders, in the order of the README's list: it stays plain; v29 to v37 put ZED and Lambda Traders on either side of one separator each (- / , ; | : ( ) and backslash): plain; v38 to v42 join ZED to Lambda Traders with a full stop, &, #, _ and an apostrophe, none a separator: inside; v43 writes LAMBDA-TRADERS ZED: the word after the name shares the part of its last word, so it is inside; v44 writes the sharp s, which case-folds to ss and finds Strasse Works; v45 writes GROSS MART, which finds the party Groß Mart; v46 writes the fi ligature, which case-folds to fi and finds Fine Foods; v47 writes the Kelvin sign, which case-folds to k and finds Kilo Works; v48 writes a dotted capital I, which decomposes to I and a combining dot; the dot after the letter is dropped, so Iota Works is found; v49 has a zero line on Sales, which its booked-to list leaves out; v50 has Lambda Traders inside and plain, and Beta Stores inside only: only Beta Stores' part is shown; v51 names a decomposed and a composed party: they are listed in the order of the names as the book writes them, the decomposed one first.",
